$Descr A4 11693 8268
Sheet 1 1
Title "PondGuard M6.3 pH AFE - PRELIMINARY"
Comment1 "AD8607 dual buffer + 1.65V bias + ADS1115 differential"
Comment2 "High impedance pH input"
Comment3 "Nernst slope is temperature dependent"
Comment4 "NOT FOR FABRICATION"
$EndDescr
Text Notes 800 900 0 100 ~ 20
PONDGUARD M6.3 - pH ANALOG FRONT-END
Text Notes 800 1350 0 65 ~ 12
3.3V -> 10k/10k DIVIDER -> AD8607A BUFFER -> VPH_BIAS ~1.65V
Text Notes 800 1800 0 65 ~ 12
VPH_BIAS -> pH REFERENCE ELECTRODE
Text Notes 800 2250 0 65 ~ 12
pH MEASUREMENT ELECTRODE -> AD8607B HIGH-Z BUFFER -> VPH_SIGNAL
Text Notes 800 2700 0 65 ~ 12
ADS1115 AIN0(+) = VPH_SIGNAL ; AIN3(-) = VPH_BIAS
Text Notes 800 3200 0 65 ~ 12
DIFFERENTIAL ADC VALUE ≈ S(T) * (7 - pH)
Text Notes 800 3650 0 65 ~ 12
S(25C) ≈ 59.16 mV/pH
Text Notes 800 4100 0 65 ~ 12
OPTIONAL OUTPUT RC: START WITH 10k + 1uF REFERENCE-INSPIRED NETWORK
Text Notes 800 4550 0 65 ~ 12
HIGH-IMPEDANCE INPUT: SHORT TRACE / GUARD / SHIELD / CLEAN PCB
Text Notes 800 5000 0 65 ~ 12
CALIBRATE AT pH 7 + pH 4 OR pH 10; USE DS18B20 FOR TEMPERATURE
Text Notes 800 5450 0 65 ~ 12
NOT FOR FABRICATION
$EndSCHEMATC
